                <pb facs="0332" n="247" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg247"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">033.4111/55: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-05-26T15:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 26, 1919, 3
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received May 26, 2.07
                            p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>2130. I am today telegraphing Mr. Lansing in Paris as follows: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“In view of the approaching visit of the Prince of Wales to Canada in
                            August, I earnestly suggest that official invitation be extended to him
                            to visit the United States. The sooner this is done the better the
                            effect.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
